On Sat, Apr 3, 2010 at 12:30 PM, Oren <get.oren@gmail.com> wrote:
> can we have a pseudocode version of the algorithm, or something similar?

For countries:

VV -> gugde'V'V
VC -> gugde'VCu
CV -> gugdeCu'V
CC -> gugdeCuCu

Codes with "h", "q", "w", "y" use "xe", "ke", "ve", "je" instead of
"xu", "ku", "vu", "ju".

For languages:

VVV -> bangV'V'V
VVC -> bangV'V'Cu
VCV -> bangVCu'V
VCC -> bangVCuCu

CVV -> banCu'V'V
CVC -> banCu'VCu
CCV -> banCuCu'V
CCC -> banCuCuCu

special case: codes that start with "n" or "g":

(n|g)VV -> baur(n|g)u'V'V
(n|g)VC -> baur(n|g)u'VCu
(n|g)CV -> baur(n|g)uCu'V
(n|g)CC -> baur(n|g)uCuCu

mu'o mi'e xorxes

